From 9ea18b2c35d3471d6a968713db46cda5286df0de Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 02:17:20 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: realtek: report actual RTL826x autonegotiated speed

rtl826x_read_status() derives speed and duplex only from the highest
common advertisement. Those abilities do not reflect a PHY downshift,
so the reported link can remain 10G or 2.5G after the physical link has
settled at a lower speed. phy_check_downshift() requires the PHY driver
to supply the actual speed and cannot detect the difference otherwise.

Read the vendor physical-status register after a successful autoneg
link-up and reuse the existing Realtek decoder, as done by the RTL822x
Clause 45 status path. The RTL8261 SDK independently reads the same
MMD31.0xa434 speed and duplex encoding. Propagate MDIO errors and leave
forced PMA configuration and the board flow_s recovery path unchanged.

This corrects status reporting; it does not establish the cause of the
observed XR1710G one-way failure. In-band USXGMII MAC speed still comes
from the PCS partner word when no separate rate-matching mode is used.

Signed-off-by: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: Codex:GPT-5.6-sol
---
 drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek_main.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek_main.c b/drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek_main.c
index 8a7b9dc..bfd795d 100644
--- a/drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/realtek/realtek_main.c
@@ -3619,6 +3619,16 @@ static int rtl826x_read_status(struct phy_device *phydev)
 			return ret;
 	}
 
+	if (phydev->link && phydev->autoneg == AUTONEG_ENABLE) {
+		/* Advertisement resolution does not reflect a downshifted link. */
+		status = phy_read_mmd(phydev, MDIO_MMD_VEND2,
+				      RTL822X_VND2_C22_REG(RTL_PHYSR));
+		if (status < 0)
+			return status;
+
+		rtlgen_decode_physr(phydev, status);
+	}
+
 	ret = genphy_c45_read_mdix(phydev);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
-- 
2.43.0

